OL,3,GNEWSA'I'm glad my miracle stroke
OL,4,Atreatment is now available 24/7'
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Gemma O'Hara woke up in the night
OL,7,Fwith "intense pain" in her neck,
OL,8,Fsickness and vertigo she knew something
OL,9,Fwas "not right".
OL,11,FThe 40-year-old had suffered a brain
OL,12,Fstem stroke, which in some cases can be
OL,13,Ffatal.
OL,15,FBut Gemma was given a medical procedure
OL,16,Fcalled a thrombectomy, which she said
OL,17,Fnot only saved her life, but was a
OL,18,F"miracle treatment" that improved her
OL,19,Frecovery.
OL,21,F"If I didn't get it in time, I wouldn't
OL,22,Fbe the way I am now."
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
